Project: Ansible Playbook Generator & Linter
Overview
The Ansible Playbook Generator & Linter is an advanced two-stage AI automation pipeline that simulates an automated infrastructure provisioning and code-review workflow. Built using Python and OpenAI (gpt-5.6-luna), the pipeline first acts as an Ansible Expert to transform natural-language task specifications into production-ready YAML playbooks, then switches into an Ansible Linter persona to rigorously audit the generated code for security, privilege escalation, and best-practice compliance.

Features
Zero-Temperature Code Generation: Configured with strict determinism (temperature=0.0) to ensure syntactically accurate Ansible playbooks using apt, service, and ufw modules.

Automated Best-Practice Auditing: Employs a specialized system persona (ansible-lint) to check for common pitfalls such as missing task names, missing privilege escalation (become: yes), and suboptimal package states (state: latest).

Strict JSON Extraction: Returns structured, machine-parsable JSON output containing exact lint error summaries (lint_errors) for continuous integration (CI) readiness.

